# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Rajni Chahal et al. (2025). Liquid–Vapor Phase Equilibrium in Molten Aluminum Chloride (AlCl3) Enabled by Machine Learning Interatomic Potentials.
#   The Journal of Physical Chemistry B. doi:10.1021/acs.jpcb.4c06450  arXiv:2410.18009v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2410.18009v1 (sha256 d4e61d678614df3c...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 337 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/chahal2025.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the PBE-D3 AIMD reference (VASP for the MLFF, CP2K for
# the NNIPs), the VASP on-the-fly MLFF (max 4,000 local reference
# configurations, 8 A cutoff) with its training and test RMSEs, and the
# DeepPot-SE models NNIP-1 and NNIP-2 (DeePMD-kit 2.1.1) used in NPT,
# two-phase coexistence and Green-Kubo viscosity MD. The NNIP validation
# errors and the 300-frame transferability force errors are reported as
# "average" or "test" errors without naming MAE or RMSE, so they are not
# encoded (gaps).

